 "summary": "Fixes an ineffective check in `mining_prioritisetransaction.py` that was intended to verify that `prioritisetransaction` causes `getblocktemplate` to return a rebuilt block. Instead of checking that the entire template changed after advancing mocktime—which always passes because the `curtime` field updates with the clock—the test now verifies that the deprioritised transaction is present before deprioritisation and absent from the template afterward.",
 "problem": "A functional test assertion intended to verify that `prioritisetransaction` triggers a block template rebuild passed trivially. Because mocktime was bumped between calls, the template's `curtime` always changed even if the cached template was reused, leaving the behavior introduced in #10196 untested against regressions.",
